---
code: K0005
title: Unterminated Raw Ident
description: "Backtick-delimited raw identifier reached the end of the line or file without a closing backtick"
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
tags: [parse, lexer, identifier, ffi]
deprecated: False
---

A raw identifier was opened with a backtick ([`` ` ``]{.expected}) but reached the end of the line (`CR`/`LF`) or end of the file without a matching closing [`` ` ``]{.expected}.

In Kura, raw identifiers are single-line tokens used primarily in `extern` declarations or member accesses when referencing C symbol names that clash with Kura keywords (such as `` `type` `` or `` `match` ``).

Example of erroneous code:

```kura
extern fn `type(ptr: c.void): c.int
```

Close the raw identifier with a matching [`` ` ``]{.expected} on the same line:

```kura
extern fn `type`(ptr: c.void): c.int
```

::: tip
Raw identifiers must contain at least one character between backticks and cannot span across newlines.
:::
